<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS4.6" class="ltx_text">V-D</span> </span><span id="S5.SS4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Utility Evaluation</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to evaluate utility preservation under different safety configurations, we conduct experiments on MMBench (See Table <a href="#S5.T4" title="TABLE IV ‣ V-D Utility Evaluation ‣ V Results and Analysis ‣ Agentic Moderation: Multi-Agent Design for Safer Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a>). The results show that models with higher capability generally exhibit stronger utility retention when safety mechanisms are applied. Advanced models such as LLaVA-1.6 and Qwe-2.5-7B maintain performance close to their vanilla setup, indicating that their safety layers impose minimal degradation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE IV: </span>Utility preservation on <span id="S5.T4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MMBench</span>. The results show minimal performance drop, demonstrating that safety components maintain strong task utility</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T4.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S5.T4.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T4.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Model</span></td>
<td id="S5.T4.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="S5.T4.4.1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> <span id="S5.T4.4.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S5.T4.4.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S5.T4.4.1.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
